    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const binary = $input.first().binary?.data;\n\nif (!binary) {\n  throw new Error('No file found');\n}\n\nconst fileName = binary.fileName;\n\nreturn [\n  {\n    json: {\n      fileName,\n      filePath: `C:\\\\SmartFileOrganizer\\\\Inbox\\\\${fileName}`,\n      mimeType: binary.mimeType,\n      fileExtension: binary.fileExtension,\n      fileSize: binary.fileSize\n    },\n    binary: {\n      data: binary\n    }\n  }\n];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -1696,
        288
      ],
      "id": "c0bb405b-2823-4550-9231-0c833e2c39ee",
      "name": "Code in JavaScript"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a file classification system.\n\nClassify the file into exactly ONE category:\n\nCareer\nFinance\nSchool\nProjects\nPersonal\nDocuments\nMedia\nOther\n\nThe most important rule:\n\nCLASSIFY THE FILE BASED ON ITS PRIMARY PURPOSE, NOT SIMPLY ON WORDS OR TOPICS FOUND INSIDE IT.\n\nFor example, a resume containing programming skills, software projects, Python, Flask, or other technical information is still CAREER because its primary purpose is to represent a person's professional qualifications.\n\nClassification guidelines:\n\n1. Career\n\nChoose Career when the file is primarily related to employment, professional work, job searching, or professional qualifications.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Resume\n* CV\n* Cover letter\n* Job application\n* Portfolio\n* Employment history\n* Work experience\n* Professional qualifications\n* Job-related certificates\n* Professional profile\n* LinkedIn-related documents\n\nIMPORTANT:\nIf a resume, CV, portfolio, or job application contains programming, software projects, technical skills, education, or work experience, classify it as CAREER, not Projects or School.\n\n2. Finance\n\nChoose Finance when the primary purpose is financial or monetary information.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Receipts\n* Invoices\n* Bills\n* Bank statements\n* Payment records\n* Budgets\n* Taxes\n* Financial reports\n* Financial transactions\n\n3. School\n\nChoose School when the primary purpose is academic or educational.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Assignments\n* Exams\n* Class notes\n* Research papers\n* Academic reports\n* School records\n* Study materials\n* Academic presentations\n\nIMPORTANT:\nA school project about programming or software is still SCHOOL if it was created primarily for academic purposes.\n\n4. Projects\n\nChoose Projects when the file is primarily part of a personal, technical, creative, or software project.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Source code\n* Project source files\n* Technical documentation\n* Software project files\n* Project specifications\n* Development notes\n* UI designs for a project\n* Project assets\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDo NOT choose Projects simply because a file mentions programming, software, coding, or technical skills.\n\n5. Personal\n\nChoose Personal when the primary purpose is personal records or private personal information.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Personal identification\n* Personal records\n* Family records\n* Personal documents\n* Private information\n* Personal correspondence\n\n6. Documents\n\nChoose Documents when the file is a general-purpose document that does not clearly belong to Career, Finance, School, Projects, or Personal.\n\n7. Media\n\nChoose Media when the file's primary purpose is media.\n\nExamples:\n\n* Photos\n* Images\n* Artwork\n* Wallpapers\n* Music\n* Audio recordings\n* Videos\n* Animations\n\nAn ordinary photo of a person, animal, object, place, food, or scenery should normally be Media unless the image is primarily a record or document belonging to another category.\n\n8. Other\n\nChoose Other only when the file cannot reasonably be classified into any of the categories above.\n\nDECISION RULES:\n\n1. Determine what the file is primarily FOR.\n2. Do not classify based only on individual keywords.\n3. Consider the entire filename and available content.\n4. If multiple categories appear in the file, choose the category representing its PRIMARY PURPOSE.\n5. Career takes priority over Projects when a resume, CV, portfolio, or job application contains technical or project information.\n6. School takes priority over Projects when a technical or programming file is primarily created for academic purposes.\n7. Media takes priority for ordinary photos, videos, and audio.\n8. Do not guess information that is not supported by the file.\n9. Choose exactly ONE category.\n\nReturn ONLY the category name.\n\nFilename:\n{{ $('Code in JavaScript').item.json.fileName }}\n\nFile type:\n{{ $('Code in JavaScript').item.json.mimeType }}\n\nFile content:\n{{ $json.text || 'No text content available.' }}\n",
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
